\tab Status: "Plain paragraphs" (yellow) when none of the markers usually used for that kind of place appears there yet; "Has special formatting" (green) when one does; "Quotation marks only" (blue) for an inscription or quotation that is only in quotation marks, with the quoted words shown; "Not drafted" when the verses have no text.\par
\tab Reference, kind and description, and which publications format the place specially.\par
\tab Suggested markers (for example \\li1 \\li2 for a genealogy, \\pc or \\sc...\\sc* for an inscription, \\qa for an acrostic) and the markers the project already uses there.\par
Filter by book, by kinds (untick the kinds you never want to see), by publication, or hide the places that are already formatted. Hide single places your team has decided about; they can be shown again at any time. Double-click a row to go to that verse in Paratext. The references are converted to the project's versification.\par
\par
\b ADD YOUR OWN PLACES\b0\par
A country, region or team can add the passages it formats in its own way (for example "Nehemiah 3: a list, format with \\li"). Click "Added places...", choose the book, references and kind, and give a source name such as "Peru". Added places appear in every project on the computer, with their own tick box in the filter. Export saves the list to a file to share; Import loads a list someone sent you.\par
\par
\b GETTING STARTED\b0\par
1. Download Install_Phils_tools.exe from the Paratext_Plugins folder, close Paratext and run it.\par
2. Tick Special Features and click "Install / update ticked" (it installs into every Paratext 9 on the computer).\par
3. Open a project and choose Tools > Special Features...\par
4. Untick the publications you do not want to follow, tick "Hide places that already have special formatting", and work through the yellow rows.\par
The window is in English, Spanish or French, following Paratext's interface language. The full user guide is SpecialFeatures_UserGuide.rtf.\par
